{"version":2,"kind":"Article","sha256":"53a91e8491a271a9de2d72fa252229241671cc2fbb5018a327d4ae2a6b928840","slug":"catechumenate","location":"/discipleship/catechumenate.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"The Catechumenate","subtitle":"Making Disciples in the Early Church","date":"2025-09-22","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Eric Araujo","given":"Eric","family":"Araujo"},"name":"Eric Araujo","corresponding":true,"email":"eric.araujo@calvin.edu","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"catechumenate.md","url":"/catechumenate-a3c1e78d9f7da95b9b9d01e0177839c9.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The catechumenate was an essential part of the early Christian community, serving as a period of instruction and preparation for new converts before their baptism. This process was not only about imparting knowledge but also about fostering spiritual growth and integration into the Christian way of life.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"cfYtgZo5Tn"}],"key":"UfTweVrQl2"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The catechumenate typically lasted for several months, during which catechumens (those preparing for baptism) would receive teachings on Christian doctrine, ethics, and practices. They would also participate in communal worship and engage in acts of charity and service.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"dPTbCRmrZJ"}],"key":"B4nGwsvFuf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To understand the catechumenate, it is important to consider its historical context. In the early centuries of Christianity, conversion to the faith was a significant decision that often involved a complete transformation of one’s life. The catechumenate provided a structured framework for this transformation, ensuring that new believers were adequately prepared for the responsibilities and challenges of Christian discipleship.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"rhDsBrefS5"}],"key":"FGz539WGsQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Roman Empire had a mentality that every citizen should be shaped through the process of education and initiation into civic life. ","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"Y8MLH6Z7sK"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paideia","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"va4aZs6Soz"}],"key":"kU0rkTrBHA"},{"type":"text","value":" was the Greek term for this process of education and formation. The catechumenate can be seen as a Christian adaptation of this broader cultural practice, where new converts were initiated into the Christian community and its values. A “Christian paideia” was being formed through the catechumenate.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"x65ISeeMT1"}],"label":"paideia","identifier":"paideia","html_id":"paideia","key":"eM9JnCHgI3"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Etymology of Catechumenate","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"X0bGMCj4Sv"}],"key":"qUAVdE7uKV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The term “catechumenate” comes from the Greek word “katecheo,” which means “to instruct” or “to teach orally,” especially in the rudiments of a subject and a skill. The term also refers to the act of reporting an important event.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"xYpEmhndOX"}],"key":"Ps4PQXGnRa"}],"class":"tip","label":"katecheo","identifier":"katecheo","html_id":"katecheo","key":"Y7QNBRELtK"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Missionary Aspect of the Catechumenate","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"CL8LQ3fBpG"}],"identifier":"the-missionary-aspect-of-the-catechumenate","label":"The Missionary Aspect of the Catechumenate","html_id":"the-missionary-aspect-of-the-catechumenate","implicit":true,"key":"d4NM89GLoY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The catechumenate was not only a process of individual transformation but also a communal and missionary endeavor. The early church saw the catechumenate as a way to nurture new believers and equip them for active participation in the life and mission of the Christian community.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"HsyLOaCL6L"}],"key":"GvDmYEN2gP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main goals were to transform the new belivers and detox them from their previous pagan formation. For that, the catechumenate focused on several key aspects:","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"lDUrxzlhfk"}],"key":"PpN2y0CxZz"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide a non polytheistic worldview","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"pDEa6FAQMl"}],"key":"BateifzgYI"},{"type":"text","value":": The catechumenate helped new converts understand the Christian worldview, which was monotheistic and centered on the worship of the one true God. This was a significant departure from the polytheistic beliefs of the surrounding culture.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"z7xIpRiaO2"}],"key":"VXBoDk26Pd"}],"key":"h5F9QvNPxC"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide a non syncretistic religious practice","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"daGza7PksN"}],"key":"jBm1ObUemr"},{"type":"text","value":": The catechumenate emphasized the distinctiveness of Christian worship and practices, helping catechumens to develop a clear understanding of Christian rituals and sacraments.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"dGBUgJbQ6s"}],"key":"n4Y9FwHaSJ"}],"key":"iQUkHSum0i"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Foster ethical transformation","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"kKzSgmD6PC"}],"key":"wOWRjTyxhx"},{"type":"text","value":": The catechumenate included teachings on Christian ethics and moral conduct, encouraging catechumens to live in accordance with the teachings of Jesus and the apostles.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"ZK7nsqrCcP"}],"key":"pGHOXDBVH1"}],"key":"KN3LgiuiLd"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable people to remain faithful in the face of persecution","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"ebtBRUvTLx"}],"key":"sfBzcRB1ro"},{"type":"text","value":": The catechumenate prepared new believers to face potential persecution and challenges to their faith, equipping them with the spiritual resources and community support needed to remain steadfast.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"yjRQQj5ndP"}],"key":"JEg9z8NhlN"}],"key":"swg4kqVIMq"}],"key":"OEXqE3Qsuq"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To detoxify new believers from their previous pagan formation, the catechumenate employed various methods, including teaching the Scriptures as a way to renarrate their lives through the Biblical stories. Also, the process of formation involved:","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"cYymXU6orM"}],"key":"pA7OAY3RwK"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"witness by one’s way of life","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"bxJzPg3RDm"}],"key":"p0fs9RVOOP"}],"key":"VOab8e5fHG"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"baptism","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"CQeuc0MEYe"}],"key":"oQfHkLLikf"}],"key":"a1eE6Z12sP"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prayer, preaching, eucharist, and other practices of the Christian community","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"ZNF1ccW0cz"}],"key":"PkY9B9aCmz"}],"key":"hGLJjXkCSb"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"witness by one’s way of life (yes, again!)","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"bRpMARQ79n"}],"key":"QoOXUKTAsS"}],"key":"z9rvItSAEm"}],"key":"HLhNotHonj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The identity formation would instill the idea that you belong to Jesus’ community, and that you are to live as a disciple of Jesus in the world. This new identity would then shape how catechumens interacted with the surrounding culture and engaged in mission. Therefore, the catechumenate can be seen as a bridge to help pagans cross over from their previous worldview and practices to a new life in Christ. At the same time, they are making their lives more attractive to the surrounding culture, as a testimony of the transforming power of the gospel.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"oSK43QDsBQ"}],"key":"tXTNc9wSUb"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Witnessing by One’s Way of Life","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"xgzGZCD7oI"}],"identifier":"witnessing-by-ones-way-of-life","label":"Witnessing by One’s Way of Life","html_id":"witnessing-by-ones-way-of-life","implicit":true,"key":"MqLtqGnrVD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One of the most powerful aspects of the catechumenate was the emphasis on witnessing by one’s way of life. Catechumens were encouraged to live out their faith in practical ways, demonstrating the transformative power of the gospel through their actions and interactions with others. This included acts of charity, hospitality, and service to those in need. By embodying the teachings of Jesus, catechumens served as living testimonies to the truth and relevance of the Christian faith.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"KeHU5oYR0N"}],"key":"NOV5piSfph"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We can attribute the growth of the early church in part to the witness of catechumens and new believers who lived out their faith in compelling ways. Their lives served as a powerful testimony to the surrounding culture, attracting others to the Christian community and inspiring them to explore the faith for themselves.","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"gqYsiB8KUL"}],"key":"LhzCZxQGlR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is quite paramount to emphasize that the early church did not grow because:","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"y9vF8OZqUw"}],"key":"cyK4dsLJMD"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"people were compelled to join through coercion or social pressure","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"Df7vmazx1w"}],"key":"OQP61bApi6"}],"key":"M9MdQetuzR"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"becoming a Christian was attractive because of material benefits or social status","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"Kcmxixzx0M"}],"key":"oPvpB4NmbK"}],"key":"gYXHYKuQEo"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"there was an organized evangelistic program to win converts","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"bS8oEKIhKw"}],"key":"bwFtf0aHDf"}],"key":"xlzhuzBr2F"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"worship services were entertaining or emotionally stimulating","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"cunOPgBhbt"}],"key":"vxQq0Lidu0"}],"key":"CLx8AQpTgq"}],"key":"CNVg5VOC4R"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The attraction were the Christians themselves, through their way of life. The early Christians demonstrated a radical commitment to love, service, and community that stood in stark contrast to the prevailing values of the Roman Empire. Their lives were marked by integrity, compassion, and a deep sense of purpose, which drew others to the faith.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"cuqDmEwAVU"}],"key":"gu6lmEWOyI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Early Christians were focused on developing practices and habits of character that would contrast with the surrounding culture.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"G4c9BiN7eM"}],"key":"pdRvqdrFCw"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Goal of Early Christian Formation from the Canons of Hippolytus","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"ko0c8Q09UX"}],"key":"ZfpnKkLduC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal is that the church “may shine with virtue, not before each other but also before the Gentiles so they may imitate them and become Christians.”","position":{"start":{"line":61,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"key":"HZ83NNEglr"}],"key":"t2EYC2CEBu"}],"class":"important","key":"N4xSMAzxkS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some of the practices that early Christians developed included:","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"Le1BA7YUhx"}],"key":"qvXdsePqrK"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"energetically feeding poor people,","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"ipiykPoEsx"}],"key":"HwzlqR1dUR"}],"key":"wPtbv4UJMX"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"providing free burial,","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"YPq23QjeZz"}],"key":"dHYdkzNcAV"}],"key":"KMz1DUTsRF"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"caring for boys and girls who lacked property and parents,","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"wxcK2VLil9"}],"key":"Ylgik0ubhQ"}],"key":"jNUMN2d7VW"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"being attentive to aged slaves, prisoners, miners, travelers,","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"p8SMCcHqmf"}],"key":"p4w0sTUDtt"}],"key":"UJ79SzWzPM"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rescuing exposed infants (often girls) from garbage heaps and raising them as their own children,","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"eY1X0Eceyf"}],"key":"tkdnugPwZD"}],"key":"R7QHk2gglU"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"caring for desperately ill pagans during the plague,","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"SD8tasoqzm"}],"key":"MPjWTBp7Di"}],"key":"AWmRWvW3nF"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"creating a ‘sociological impossibility’ by breaking barriers between rich/poor, male/female, slave/free, Greek/barbarian,","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"d5TqWERrWm"}],"key":"e48Fnrnw0n"}],"key":"rj5z21TPAz"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"radiating hope and joy in a culture of despair, anxiety, uncertainty,","position":{"start":{"line":73,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"key":"ATI9aj0bI5"}],"key":"hHJSnhQHbJ"}],"key":"qxaF8Z8mtp"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"practicing chastity / marital faithfulness in sex-saturated culture,","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"GUNAsdOKmw"}],"key":"i6mTCnf6mn"}],"key":"aKtighVErz"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"simplicity and generosity amidst consumption and accumulation,","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"WWqjL6MUw3"}],"key":"PJAXmYT2ah"}],"key":"RiVnL8YqOb"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"forgiving their executioners.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"oB2ffQCdbe"}],"key":"RQRxzTEM2Y"}],"key":"PycvxfheXe"}],"key":"M2IQsOroVb"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Process of the Catechumenate","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"QD3Vpg87Uc"}],"identifier":"the-process-of-the-catechumenate","label":"The Process of the Catechumenate","html_id":"the-process-of-the-catechumenate","implicit":true,"key":"XlUNyGTnrd"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The catechumenate typically involved several stages, including:","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"CcffgTbJvq"}],"key":"jmg9aE94Px"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inquiry","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"YDk8HWnMuU"}],"key":"YmzJwO1Q2a"},{"type":"text","value":": Individuals interested in becoming Christians would express their desire to join the faith community. They would meet with church leaders and receive initial instruction on the basics of Christian belief and practice.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"szHXR0H4V9"}],"key":"R1vvgjlq2p"}],"key":"RwnM3Ub8Ep"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Catechesis","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"kC78Pg8dYv"}],"key":"i937T2bZUN"},{"type":"text","value":": This was the main perio